From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: caskade <caskade@localhost>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 11:45:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Text fields: read-only, passwords, copying, single-line
 paste, commands

- A `readonly` field takes no edits (typing, delete, cut, paste, an IME's
  composition, Cocoa's edit commands) but still selects and copies; the
  IME isn't enabled on it. It was editable like any other field.
- A password field doesn't copy or cut its text to the clipboard.
- Copying no longer fires `input`, and an empty cut does nothing.
- Shortcuts match whatever Shift or Caps Lock did to the letter: Ctrl+C
  with Caps Lock on copied nothing.
- A single-line field drops pasted line breaks, as browsers do.
- `BaseDocument::text_field_command` (select all, copy, cut, paste) runs a
  field's edit commands for a context menu or a gamepad, with the events
  they generate.

The field's flags are read from its attributes when each event arrives.
Tests in `text_input_clipboard.rs`.
